ur  mobile device or your laptop be edgy  sweet neat or on the big screen to  present your view in Google slides it  gives you as a presenter a special view  into the presentation the presenter view  helps you be a better presenter with  features like speaker notes quick slide  validation and a laser pointer  speaker notes allow you to craft your  message and have access to all the notes  you need to give a great presentation  right at your fingertips our quick nav  ik navigation tools and presenter view  allow you to quickly navigate to any  slide in your deck if you need to  revisit a specific point or visual and  at any time you can turn on a laser  pointer to direct your the attention of  your your audience to a certain part of  the presentation  in presenter view you also have access  to a feature unique to Google slides Q&amp;A  with Q&amp;A you can better engage your  audience by allowing them to submit  questions and vote on them during Google  slides presentations once you start a  Q&amp;A session  Sly's displays a unique URL that  audience members can go to and submit  questions you can decide when to answer  the questions and display them right on  the big screen one by one the audience  members can also vote on the questions  other people submit so you know where to  focus your time if you only have a few  minutes for questions this concludes the  journey of a typical presentation I hope  you learned some about about some size  features you may not have been aware of  and as a quick recap slides helps you  get started with tools like templates  and AP is and facilitates real-time  collaboration with comments and action  items you can let slides for your  personal designer with slides Explorer  and finally you can have confidence with  slides to help to help you that help  give you that the power to give a great  presentation and host live Q&amp;A with an  audience if you want to learn more about  Google slides you can visit the G suite  Learning Center t